From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:33:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] vdin: capture one eye of a frame packed output

A frame packed 3D output stacks both eyes with a blank between them in
one tall frame. A capture squeezed the whole stack into its image, so
the LEDs and screenshots showed two squashed pictures.
---
 drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_drv.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_drv.c b/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_drv.c
--- a/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_drv.c
@@ -0,6 +0,10 @@
 {
 	const struct vinfo_s *vinfo = get_current_vinfo();
 
+	/* frame packing stacks the eyes with a blank between them: take the first */
+	if (vinfo->info_3d == FP_3D)
+		return vinfo->height - vinfo->vtotal / 2;
+
 	return vdin_v4l2_is_field(devp) ? vinfo->field_height : vinfo->height;
 }
 
